Authors: Mark Alan Lilly
Series: beyond PTSD
Collection: A Way Out
Wherein: Wherein i admit that the best therapy for me is to help others who suffer these ravages too...

overveiw

+ moving
+ helping
+ breathing
+ loving (prphylactically when there is no other option)


###movement

my kind of ptsd has always been of the more hyper-vigilant variety, where i need to keep moving to feel safer. my bags remain packed no matter where i spend the night, be it the home of my wife and children or on the road somewhere on this vast, fascinating planet. my bags are always packed, i have my emergency stash of cash, passport and eyeglasses close at hand. 

i think a large part of this stems from the fact that my nightmares began when i was invaded at age 18, and part of me froze there never to mature. being 18 is, or was, for me, a time of motion, of moving away from parents and toward my own independent life. It was moving north, moving around my new hometown with a freedom i had always dreamed about. the robbery froze me there and ever since, my bags are packed and movement makes me feel safer—after all, a moving, zig-zagging, unpredictable target is far harder to snipe.

###for movement's sake

but running away is futile, b/c the demons always know where i am, often before i do, laying in wait to ambush.

so what to do?

how to move forward when everywhere is a trap waiting to claw through your meager defenses and have their way with you.

###show up

Help out, anywhere you can, b/c we're not alone we who have survived the terrors.

breathe to make space, and in that space look up, and with that small moment of clarity, realize there are others here who suffer more, who know not the space between the breath, who can't conceive of anything but bringing all this to an end. 

show up for yourself by showing up for others. The demons hate that and they will fight back, lie to you more viciously, demean your motivations, belittle your actions but dig deeper, stand strong, this is a way out.

###salvation

Fellow travelers of the dark valleys of despair, help out. Find anyone who suffers too and stand by them, watch their back for a moment even if you cannot let down your guard, use that to guard someone else so they can change their socks without fear of imminent attack.

go sit with someone who has an untold story to tell and let their words come toward you and listen if you can, but scan the horizon and hear their heart breaking and know that we can be kind simply by refusing to let each other feel utterly alone.

Show up, for yourself and others in the same breath, b/c alone, we can never guard our own back, but together, there's a small chance and every chance for a moment's peace must be cherished and revered and striven for b/c bodymind wants to feel you and smell flowers and live in amazing ways, and while we live, we can never forget that, b/c we come from Love and Love wants to live out its own life right here on this crazy planet.

Help out, show up, stand strong, breathe deep and never let down your guard, but guard others until maybe one day you can stand down too and feel peace. If not, or if so, show up for someone else. It's the only way out.



